  "details": "Tested with VRCSDK 3.10.3.\n\nI would like to report an issue with `VRCJson.TryDeserializeFromJson`.\n\nIt appears that deserialization fails when a JSON array contains string values with bracket characters such as `{`, `}`, `[`, `]`, and the number of opening and closing brackets inside those strings does not match, even though the JSON itself is valid.\n\nThe following are valid JSON arrays and should deserialize successfully:\n\n```\n\n[\"[\"]\n\n```\n\n```\n\n[\"{\"]\n\n```\n\n`VRCJson.TryDeserializeFromJson` returns `false` for these examples.\n\nThere is also a case where malformed JSON arrays are incorrectly accepted as valid.\n\n```\n\n[ [ } ]\n\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```\n\nstring json1 = @\"[\"\"[\"\"]\";\n\nDebug.Log(VRCJson.TryDeserializeFromJson(json1, out var _1));\n\n// expect: True\n\n// actual: False\n\n```\n\n```\n\nstring json2 = \"[[}]\";\n\nDebug.Log(VRCJson.TryDeserializeFromJson(json2, out var _2));\n\n// expect: False\n\n// actual: True\n\n```",
  "error": null,
